  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: `xs.first() == Present { value: X }` answers false when the list's first element is X. Two optionals compared, both meaning Present X, and the interpreter answers unequal. The comparison is T? == T?, so the wall of optional_compared_with_required_value (EqualityOptionalityMismatch, gunbc#13179) admits it, correctly: it has one meaning.",

    "ROOT, NOT A NEW EVALUATOR DEFECT: the interpreter realizes `first` as the raw element or Null, while emitted Rust realizes it as Optional<T> (gunbc.cli_dispatch_surface; test.claim.cli_dispatch_surface interpreter_first_returns_the_modeled_optional was the known-red specimen). The read hands equality a bare X, the literal is Present X, and equality answers by representation, the arm optional_compared_with_required_value already records. So the earliest unjustified boundary (DESIGN 6b) is the interpreter's `first` producing a value that is not the modeled optional. Equality and the checker are downstream consequences.",

    "WHAT THIS ROW ADDS IS THE HARM ROUTE. EqualityOptionalityMismatch tells the author to compare against `Present { value: .. }` first, so following the compiler's own remedy for a refused T? == T walks straight into this divergence and gets a silently false Bool. Measured 2026-10-07 on gunbc.os_install_actuator_selection srv3_os_install_actuator_host_selected_because_requirements_and_policy: rewritten that way, the production predicate went false. gunbc#13536 matches on the optional instead.",

    "EVIDENCE BY EXECUTION: test.claim.optional_equality_by_representation. RED a_present_first_equals_its_present_literal is `.first()` over a data list of variant rows, compared with a Present literal. It is held known-red in v2.workflow.floor_expected_red and STAYS there: it is not executed true (below). The row is deleted by the PR that executes it true, and the claim then remains as the permanent regression control (DESIGN 4b(4)). EXECUTED (srv2, head 8941390fdf37, `gunbc run --claim-run` on test.claim.interpreter_list_read_optional_witness, after binary sha256 41ed1bb656e5a9031b1a1e3e657dce5bbdc4e634cd8656b9c764a36a032e6cd8 built 2026-11-01T14:53:37Z): after 16 PASS / 0 FAIL; origin/main binary sha256 47e6c33e20d7ceab7c8bcf109b26d49556d4a53ad18c989df0d37139d0b45711 5 PASS / 10 FAIL (first/last/get, map get, none-field REDs), plus a Null-field evaluation error at the prior head 5dfd470f0d51. STANDING: interpreter route of list first/last/get executed (rung moved by that receipt); this file's own claims did not resolve under claim-run on either binary (type/closure error, pre-existing), so they carry no executed receipt; the emitted-Rust route is not covered by this run. POSITIVE CONTROL a_match_on_the_present_first_reads_its_value is the same read eliminated by a match, an ordinary claim. First observed as probes zz_a1 (FAIL) and zz_c1 (PASS) over test.claim.os_install_actuator_selection at gunbc#13536's base.",

    "2026-10-09, PR #13607: the ETHTOOL_GCHANNELS reply decoder compared numbers.first() against Present containing the command string. The live ABI probe returned the correct nine u32s, and all numeric checks passed, but the valid-reply witness failed because this comparison answered false for 60 against Present 60. The decoder follows the existing match discipline; its positive count, wrong-command, malformed and foreign-interface controls remain enrolled. This repairs that consumer, not the seed's known representation divergence.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder on the interpretation path. CEILING: 4. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: one authority for `first` from which the interpreter and the emitted realization are both derived, so the interpreter's `first` yields the modeled optional on every route (method form and pipe form). This PR authors that climb for the interpreter route: both claims (this one and interpreter_first_returns_the_modeled_optional) are expected to pass once they execute, and their roster rows are deleted by the PR that executes them true, the claims remaining as regression controls (DESIGN 4b(4)); the rung moves only on an executed receipt, and the interpreter route has one (STANDING above); the emitted route has none. Until the emitted route is covered, the interim discipline at a `first` read is to match on the optional.",
    "2026-10-17, S0 of the nameless-type-leaf program: the same fork on the TYPE axis. `T?` (the payload type carrying CardOptional) and the std.optional coproduct `Optional<P>` are one type, and v1.compiler.infer_types node_type_compatible answered false for the pair, so `let c: T? = if n == 0 { Absent } else { <Optional<T>> }` (std.source_annotation annotation_gap_in) was refused once a bare Absent took its expected `T?`. REPAIR AT THE COMPARISON AUTHORITY, NOT THE JOIN: node_type_compatible relates a CardOptional leaf to Optional<P> exactly when P is identical to the leaf's required form (applied_argument_types_identical, identity not compatibility). S0 repairs T?/Optional<P> compatibility at the shared comparison authority. Mixed application-versus-non-application equality remains unsupported and returns false regardless of attached resolution. No expansion-recovery or positional fallback remains. Supporting that equality requires retained instantiation evidence, deferred until a consumer needs it. NEXT RUNG, A: a retained-instantiation carrier on the generic expansion (generic_declaration_application would keep the arguments, the arm would compare them directly); TRIGGER: a consumer needs application-vs-expansion equality (the #14152 census admitted 0 of 104 Coproduct-vs-Node rows, so none does today). EVIDENCE BY EXECUTION: test.claim.optional_leaf_instance_join_witness is true on the repaired mirror and false against main's, and its refusal twin (payload String against Int?) still refuses. Self-host closure and binary are byte-identical to main under the relation.",
